hadiths[32]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3790","Ishaq bin Bahlwal narrates: I said to Sufyan: If a person is not the girl's peer in terms of position, can a person marry his (sister) to a pious (poor, or family status) person? He replied yes."
"3791","Shaykh Ibn Abi Laili says: Kafu will be considered in religion and position, and Ka'i narrates: I heard Imam Abu Hanifa (RA) saying that Kafu will be considered in religion, position, and wealth."
"3792","Sha'bi narrated: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have married (your wives to) Muqdad and Zayd, because the most honorable among you in the sight of Allah is the one whose morals are the best."
"3793","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Abu Hind, a slave of Banubaydah, used to follow the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He followed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever wants to see a person in whose heart Allah has engraved faith should look at Abu Hind. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) also said: Marry her (your female relative) and establish a relationship with her."
"3794","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: Abu Hind put his heels on the blessed head of the Prophet (PBUH), then the Prophet (PBUH) said: O Banu Biyadha, marry Abu Hind and marry him (to one of your daughters)."
"3795","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Whoever wants to see a person whose heart has been enlightened by Allah with faith, let him see Abu Hind. The narrator narrates: That person used to work as a backhoe."
"3796","Sayyidah Zainab bint Jahsh (RA) narrates: Some people from Quraysh sent me a message of marriage, so I sent my sister Hamna bint Jahsh (RA) to the Prophet (SAW) to consult him about it. The Prophet (SAW) said to her: Why does she not marry the man who taught her the Book of her Lord and the Sunnah of her Prophet? Did you find out, O Messenger of Allah! Who is that person? The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Zayd bin Haritha, then Hamna got angry, he said: O Messenger of Allah, will you marry your cousin with your (freed, former) slave? Sayyidah Zainab (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Hamna came to me and told me about this, so I became more angry with her and I used harsher words than her, so Allah revealed this verse: “No believing man or woman (does not have authority) that when Allah and His Messenger give a decision in a matter, they have the authority (to act differently from this decision) in this matter.” Sayyida Zainab (RA) narrates: I sent a message to the Prophet (PBUH) asking him to marry me to whomever he wishes. The Prophet (PBUH) married me to Zayd bin Haritha (RA). Fear Allah. After that he mentioned the rest of the hadith."
"3797","Hanzalah bin Abu Sufyan narrates the statement of his mother: Sayyidna Abd al-Rahman bin Awf's sister was the wife of Sayyidna Bilal."
"3798","Narrated by Sayyiduna Samurah: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Wealth is according to wealth, and charity is piety."
"3799","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said, \It is according to wealth"," and kindness is piety.\"""""
"3800","Sayyiduna Abi Bin Ka'b Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: I asked, O Messenger of Allah, is the ruling of this verse common to a divorced woman and a widow? The Prophet (PBUH) inquired: In which verse? I said: (This verse) And the Idda of pregnant women will end when they give birth to a child. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said yes."
"3801","Sayyiduna Abi bin Ka'b (RA) narrates: He asked the Prophet (PBUH) about this verse: And the ``Idah of pregnant women will end when they give birth to a child.'' Is it for Yabih? The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that it is for both the triple talaq woman and the widow."
"3802","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): A woman is married for four reasons: her wealth, her lineage, her piety and her beauty."
"3803","Sayyidina Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: A woman is married for three reasons: her wealth, her beauty, and her religion."
"3804","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (PBUH): A man's dignity is his religion, his greatness is his intellect and his virtue is his morals."
"3805","Abdullah bin Baridah quotes the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding his father: According to the people of the world, the standard of excellence is wealth."
"3806","Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, says: The virtue of a man is his religion, his morals, and his essence (goodness) is his intellect."
"3807","Sayyiduna Umar (may God be pleased with him) says: Bravery and cowardice are inherent in men, while the same is the case with karma and custom."
"3808","Amr ibn Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: A woman came to the service of the Prophet (peace be upon him) and said: This is my son. My stomach was a vessel for him, my bosom was a shelter for him, my breast was a source of water for him, and now his father wants to separate him from me. would do"
"3809","Amr bin Shu'ayb, on the authority of his father, narrates this statement of his grandfather: A woman had a quarrel with her (former) husband about her child, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman has more right to (raise) her children until she (remarries)."
"3810","Amr bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: A woman came to the Prophet's service and said: O Messenger of Allah, my stomach was a vessel for her, my breast was a source of irrigation for her, and my lap was a shelter for her."
"3811","Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Indeed, a person will be given a grace period of one year."
"3812","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"3813","Saeed bin Musayb says about a person who cannot have intercourse with his wife: He will be given a grace period of up to one year."
"3814","Sayyiduna Abdullah Radiyallahu Anhu says: Such a person will be given respite for one year, if he is able to have intercourse, then it is fine, otherwise the husband and wife will be separated."
"3815","Abu Nu'man narrates: We came to the service of Sayyidna Mughira bin Shuba Radiyallahu Anhu to inquire about the person in question, and he said that he will be given a grace period of one year."
"3816","Sayyidna Mughira bin Shuba Radiyallahu Anhu says: A one-year respite will be given to a person who is responsible."
"3817","Sayyidna Mughira bin Shuba (RA) says: A one-year grace period will be given to the person concerned and it will be calculated from the day when the woman filed the case. Abd al-Rahman says: Sufyan Thauri and Imam Malik have given this fatwa (the deadline will start from the day on which) the woman filed the case."
"3818","Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says: When the door is closed and the veil is pulled down, the payment of dowry becomes obligatory."
"3819","Hazrat Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: When a man closes the door and lowers the veil or looks at a woman's seventy, it will be necessary to pay dowry on her."
"3820","Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says: When a man closes the door and lowers the veil or looks at a woman's seventy, it becomes obligatory to pay dowry on her."
"3821","The same has been narrated about Sayyiduna Umar (RA) and Sayyidna Ali (RA)."
